<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Karachay-Cherkessia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Karachay-Cherkessia is a republic of the Russian Federation in the north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasus">Caucasus</a>, with its capital at Cherkessk. It is home mainly to the Turkic Karachays, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/circassians">Cherkess</a> (Circassians), the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abazins">Abazins</a> and Russians. Created as an autonomous region in 1922, it was divided when the Karachays were deported to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a> in 1943, reunited after their return in 1957, and became a republic in 1992.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/karachay-cherkessia.jpg" alt="Karachay-Cherkessia" width="320" height="176" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: File:Map of Russia (2014–2022) - Karachay-Cherkessia.svg: Stasyan117 derivative work: Seryo93 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_Russia_(2014%E2%80%932022)_-_Karachay-Cherkessia_(Crimea_disputed).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
